<%- include('./partials/header.ejs') %>

    <!--FAQs-->
    <div class="container px-0 py-3" id="FAQs">
        <div class="row p-4 pb-3 pe-lg-0 pt-lg-5 align-items-center rounded-3 border shadow-lg" id="content">
            <h1 class="display-6 fw-bold lh-1 ">FAQs</h1>
            <div class="card-flip">
                <div class="card-flip-inner">
                    <div class="card-front">
                        <h5>What is UV Index?</h5>
                        <span class="symbol">+</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card-back show">
                        <p>The UV Index is an international scale that measures the intensity of ultraviolet (UV)
                            radiation from the sun. A higher UV Index means a greater risk of skin and eye damage,
                            so more protection is recommended.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-flip">
                <div class="card-flip-inner">
                    <div class="card-front">
                        <h5>What UV level is considered dangerous?</h5>
                        <span class="symbol">+</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card-back">
                        <p>A UV Index of 6 or higher is considered high. At these levels, prolonged sun exposure can
                            increase the risk of sunburn and skin damage. Wearing sunscreen, protective clothing,
                            and sunglasses is recommended.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-flip">
                <div class="card-flip-inner">
                    <div class="card-front">
                        <h5>Do I need sunscreen on cloudy days?</h5>
                        <span class="symbol">+</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card-back">
                        <p>Yes, you should still use sunscreen on cloudy days. UV rays can penetrate through clouds
                            and cause skin damage, even when it's not sunny.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-flip">
                <div class="card-flip-inner">
                    <div class="card-front">
                        <h5>How often should I reapply sunscreen?</h5>
                        <span class="symbol">+</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card-back">
                        <p>It is recommended to reapply sunscreen every two hours, or more frequently if you are
                            swimming or sweating.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-flip">
                <div class="card-flip-inner">
                    <div class="card-front">
                        <h5>Can UV rays harm my eyes?</h5>
                        <span class="symbol">+</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card-back">
                        <p>Yes, UV rays can harm your eyes. Prolonged exposure to UV radiation can lead to
                            cataracts, corneal damage, and other eye conditions. It's important to wear sunglasses
                            that block UV rays to protect your eyes.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-flip">
                <div class="card-flip-inner">
                    <div class="card-front">
                        <h5>What SPF should I use?</h5>
                        <span class="symbol">+</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card-back">
                        <p>It is recommended to use a broad-spectrum sunscreen with an SPF of at least 30. This will
                            provide adequate protection against both UVA and UVB rays.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card-flip">
                <div class="card-flip-inner">
                    <div class="card-front">
                        <h5>How does SunSafe calculate the UV Index?</h5>
                        <span class="symbol">+</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card-back">
                        <p>SunSafe uses your current location (with your permission) and retrieves real-time UV data
                            from the OpenUV API to provide personalized UV information and recommendations.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        const quest = document.querySelectorAll(".card-front");

        quest.forEach(question => {
        question.addEventListener("click", () => {

            const answer = question.nextElementSibling;
            const symbol = question.querySelector(".symbol");
    
            answer.classList.toggle("show");
    
            if (answer.classList.contains("show")) {
                symbol.textContent = "−";   // Minus sign
            } else {
                symbol.textContent = "+";
            }

            }); 
        });

    </script>

    <%- include('./partials/footer.ejs') %>